Implemented **DET.CHART.ALT_SUMMARY** as a deterministic accessibility check for charts and graphs.

## Rule signal (from source)

Pass when a chart/graph has at least one of:
- Text summary (`aria-label`, `alt`, `title`, sr-only summary)
- `aria-describedby` / `aria-labelledby` pointing to substantive text
- Nearby caption (`figcaption`, preceding KS `<p class="forge-support">`, etc.)

## What changed

### 1. `design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-chart-alt-summary.check.js`
Replaced the stub with a full check following the `det-card-title` pattern:

- **`MIN_CHART_SUMMARY_CHARS = 8`** — minimum summary length
- **Chart roots:** `[data-ks-chart]`, `.ks-chart-mount`, `[data-chart]`, chart containers, sized `canvas`/`svg[role="img"]` inside chart contexts
- **Exclusions:** ambient layers (`.forge-ambient-bg`, `.forge-aurora`, etc.), `aria-hidden`, tiny/decorative canvases
- **Summary detection:** aria attributes, hidden summaries, `figure > figcaption`, adjacent caption paragraphs (matches KS chart mount pattern)
- **Exports:** `rule`, `findingsFromChartAltSummaryReport`, `collectChartAltSummaryReport`, `run(ctx)`

Metadata: `area: accessibility`, `scoreDimension: accessibilitySemanticsMeta`, `defaultSeverity: major`, `priorityWeight: 7`.

### 2. `design-rules/blender/rule-mappings.js`
Registered under `DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS` with `status: 'implemented'`.

### 3. `auditor-tests/det-chart-alt-summary.test.js`
Unit tests for constants, finding shape, empty report, and `metrics.chartAltSummaryReport` wiring.

### 4. `design-rules/registry.generated.json`
Already reflects `status: "implemented"` with the correct metadata for this rule.

